      "section": "Measurements",
      "order": 2,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "center",
      "body": "One card per measurement, each carrying the summary its own shape calls for: a box plot where the spread matters, a two-column stat grid where the quartiles do, a histogram where the shape is bimodal, and a threshold count where the question is really \"how many are above the line\". Four layouts on four columns of the same table \u2014 the point is that the layout follows the column, not the other way round.",
      "wf_tag": "python/iris_workflow"
    },
